<article class="env-definition" id="065I">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/065I">Definition <span data-tag="065I">15.83.4</span>.</a> Let $R \to A$ be a finite type ring map. Let $K^\bullet $ be a complex of $A$-modules. Let $M$ be an $A$-module. Let $m \in \mathbf{Z}$. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
We say $K^\bullet $ is <em>$m$-pseudo-coherent relative to $R$</em> if the equivalent conditions of Lemma <a href="/tag/065H" data-tag="065H">15.83.3</a> hold. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We say $K^\bullet $ is <em>pseudo-coherent relative to $R$</em> if $K^\bullet $ is $m$-pseudo-coherent relative to $R$ for all $m \in \mathbf{Z}$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We say $M$ is <em>$m$-pseudo-coherent relative to $R$</em> if $M[0]$ is $m$-pseudo-coherent relative to $R$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We say $M$ is <em>pseudo-coherent relative to $R$</em> if $M[0]$ is pseudo-coherent relative to $R$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>